.TH PAPERWEIGHT\-THEME 1 "2026-06-19" "paperweight-skel 0.2.57" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperweight\-theme \- apply a PaperweightOS color theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperweight\-theme
.RI [ theme ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperweight\-theme
switches the active color theme across all desktop components atomically:
sway colors, waybar styles, swaync, gtklock, wofi, and the foot terminal.
.PP
With no argument, a
.BR wofi (1)
picker lists the available themes for interactive selection.
.PP
Only one theme switch runs at a time.
If a switch is already in progress when
.B paperweight\-theme
is called again, the new theme name is queued and applied after the running
switch completes.
.PP
When the invoking user is in the
.B sudo
group, the login screen (gtkgreet), GRUB, and Plymouth themes are also
updated via
.BR paperweight-set-greeter-theme (8),
.BR paperweight-grub-theme (8),
and
.BR paperweight-plymouth-theme (8)
respectively.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I theme
Name of the theme to apply.
If omitted, a wofi picker is shown.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway/themes/
Sway color variable files
.RI ( <name>.conf ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/waybar/themes/
Waybar CSS palette and module style files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaync/themes/
Swaync notification center CSS files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gtklock/themes/
Gtklock screen locker CSS files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/wofi/themes/
Wofi launcher CSS files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/foot/themes/
Foot terminal color INI files.
.TP
.I ~/.config/paperweight-os/active-theme
Records the name of the currently active theme.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/paperweight-os/theme-switch.log
Timestamped log of all theme switch operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paperweight-set-greeter-theme (8),
.BR paperweight-grub-theme (8),
.BR paperweight-plymouth-theme (8),
.BR waybar-theme-status (1),
.BR wofi (1)
